{
  "id": "old-intake",
  "name": "The Old Intake",
  "description": "The old intake under Pump House Nine, below where the shift goes: a low vault of stained concrete and rusted iron under sweating live mains, cold teal coming down through a ceiling grating from the settling water. A heavy steel door stands ajar on the left beside a yellow bulkhead lamp and a junction box. In the middle, the huge round mouth of the dead intake pipe, its gate hanging open, green marker lamps running away into the dark. On the right, a hatch seized with rust, and on an old pump plinth a bedroll, boots, a water bottle and a few tins under a caged work lamp.",
